Recover complete messages from an arbitrarily divided byte stream (@computing-message-framing: 0, is #chapter, #hephaestus-core "Reason-from-missing-replies-without-inventing-remote-observations.lingua#r_008C1CDFEA1BACFF3D8BA60B87") { r_004304223020FC2B4C22A527DB
We define an original wire format for a simulated accounting service. A frame begins with two bytes representing payload length in unsigned big-endian order: bytes a,b represent 256a+b. A request payload is exactly three bytes: kind 1, identity 1 through 255, amount 1 through 15. A result payload is exactly four bytes: kind 2, identity 1 through 255, then an unsigned two-byte cumulative count 0 through 65535. These are teaching limits and meanings, not a public Internet protocol. Zero is unavailable as an operation identity. A result can encode zero even though our positive-only workload never produces it.

For request identity 1, amount 2, the decimal bytes are [0,3,1,1,2]. The corresponding result count 2 is [0,4,2,1,0,2]. Concatenating them produces eleven bytes. A receiver may get all eleven together, one at a time, or any of the 2¹⁰ divisions at the ten internal boundaries. Recovering the same two messages in every case is a meaningful requirement. Counting byte positions does not involve character encoding: these fields are binary integers, not decimal text.

The decoder retains a pending prefix. After two bytes it rejects lengths other than three or four. It then waits for exactly the declared payload, validates the kind, exact length and field ranges, emits one typed tuple and clears the prefix. It continues through any remaining bytes. An empty chunk changes nothing. End of input is successful only between frames; one pending header byte, or a complete header with incomplete payload, is a truncated stream. A kind/length disagreement is malformed, not a partial message to reinterpret under another type.

Prove chunk independence on valid input by induction on bytes consumed. Before each next byte, the pending buffer is exactly the suffix after the last complete frame; the emitted sequence consists of the complete valid frames before it. The next byte either extends that suffix or completes its uniquely determined length. The action depends on this prefix and byte, never on the containing chunk. Thus all chunk partitions give the same outputs. The retained partial buffer has at most five bytes: a six-byte result frame is emitted as soon as its final byte arrives. The returned list for one enormous chunk can still be enormous; bounded partial buffering is not a bound on all allocations or caller input size.

The supplied decoder closes on malformed wire input. It does not search for a convenient next header, because arbitrary data could imitate one. Its call returns completed tuples only if that call succeeds; if a later frame in the same chunk is malformed, earlier local tuples from that failed call are discarded. Chunk independence is therefore claimed for valid complete streams, not for side effects on partially valid failing streams. An application must specify its own per-message transaction and error policy. Never apply effects while merely collecting an incomplete frame.

[Remote Procedure Call Protocol Specification Version 2 RFC 5531](../sources/Remote-Procedure-Call-Protocol-Specification-Version-2-RFC-5531.lingua#r_0058E17EDA89658DCF6713FD72) section 11 provides a contrasting real record-delimiting convention. Its format is different; our small codec neither implements ONC RPC nor conforms to its record marking. Read the selected standard only after reconstructing this original example. Compare field widths and fragmentation without copying a standard's structure into a claim of interoperability.

**Work:** decode [0,4,2,7,1,2] and explain why its value is 258. Reject [0,3,2,7,2] even though every byte is individually in range. Give a truncated prefix whose next byte could complete it. Derive the partition count for a nonempty n-byte stream. Run the study's exhaustive partitions and length checks, then extend the schema with a unit/version field and state how both peers distinguish it before interpreting an amount.

**Continue:** [Reason from missing replies without inventing remote observations](Reason-from-missing-replies-without-inventing-remote-observations.lingua#r_008C1CDFEA1BACFF3D8BA60B87).

**Return:** [Computing](../Computing.lingua#r_02FE84C805C79A9D396F478641).
